[Q23-D4] Fan(tau,L) slack = L-1 ?  (symbolic check + explicit instances)
   In Fan(tau,L): every b in B_lo is B-universal with deg_A(b)=1, so deg(b)=(tau-1)+1=tau;
   nu = 1 (B = K_tau - uv).  slack = L(tau+1) - (L*tau + 1) = L - 1.
   verified as an identity for tau=4..8, L=1..tau-1: slack == L-1 everywhere.

