   squeeze => Sum deg_A = 2 forced

[Q23-D2] Theorem MB's 'every such b lies in B_lo+' vs the draft's own Prop L2 config
   Prop L2(d): T1={u}, T2={v} with u,v in B_hi.  B_lo+ subset B_lo, and B_hi cap B_lo = {}.
   => u,v in T1 u T2 but u,v NOT in B_lo+: the universally-quantified sentence is false as written.
   The count only uses c = |B_lo cap (T1 u T2)|, and B_lo cap (T1 u T2) subset B_lo+ IS true,
   so the inequality |B_lo+| + c + mbar <= L + nu(B_lo) - 1 is unaffected.
